    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup today is headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 73.49 score makes him our premier start against Fisher. A massive 14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against the right-hander, paired with a favorable park and solid order position, provides the highest floor on the roster. **Drake Baldwin** also warrants high-leverage expectations (68.74); his matchup against Rodriguez offers an elite SP skill advantage (+17%), which effectively mitigates the risk of starting a catcher in a high-variance slot. We are similarly leaning into **Sam Antonacci** (62.70) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.37), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against right-handed pitching, with **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s leadoff spot providing the necessary volume to hunt for the stolen bases we desperately need to climb the 5x5 standings.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved the marginal starts at the corner infield and middle infield spots. **Jacob Wilson** (61.84) ultimately squeezed into the MI slot due to a park factor bump and an assumed #2 spot in the order, narrowly edging out **Jackson Merrill** (49.73). **Jackson Merrill** fell victim to a tough matchup against Cantillo and a significant dynamic platoon penalty (-13%), forcing him to the bench in favor of higher-efficiency hitters. We remain cautious regarding **Gunnar Henderson** (42.46) and **Coby Mayo** (43.35); both are facing Seymour, whose elite skill set forces a double-digit penalty to their base projections. While we need their upside, their scores are hovering dangerously close to our \"Below floor\" threshold.\n\nLooking at the periphery, monitor the lineup status for **Jacob Wilson** and **Wade Meckler** closely; both are currently projected based on historical batting orders. Should either be dropped in the lineup, their efficiency scores will shift immediately. Furthermore, while **Andy Pages** sits at 49.12, his matchup against Misiorowski is fraught with danger\u2014a 2.03 xERA is the toughest test for any hitter on our roster today. The only saving grace for **Andy Pages** is a wind-aided environment (+5%), but he remains the most volatile asset in today's lineup. With **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jordan Westburg** all unavailable due to rest or IL, the Waves must rely on our depth to squeeze value out of these moderate matchups.",
